@startuml
' Figure 23-2: the corrupted-sigma probe as a sequence. The decisive "replacement, not duplicate"
' evidence: corrupt the Dovetail report's sigma (the redex locator) leaving only the GATE fields
' valid, run the MATCH path, and observe the CORRECT reduct re-sourced from the SPREAD of the
' structurally reflected subject. Worked base redex: Swap(A, B) ~> Pair(B, A).
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName monospaced
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #4A5568
  LifeLineBorderColor #7A7A7A
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F4F4F4
  ParticipantBorderColor #7A7A7A
  ParticipantFontColor #202020
}

title Figure 23-2 — the corrupted-<latex>\sigma</latex> probe: corrupt the report, still-correct OUT re-sourced from the spread\nWorked redex  Swap(A, B) ~> Pair(B, A)   (base; every family runs the same shape)

participant "test\nharness" as T #EBF3FE
participant "Dovetail report\n(compile-time)" as R #FDECD9
participant "MATCH invocation\nrho_net_match_invocation_\nfrom_dovetail_to" as M #E8F0FE
participant "f1r3node reducer\n(RSpace, in Rho)" as RHO #E6F4EA
participant "@OUT\n(observed reduct)" as OUT #FEF7E0

T -> R : dovetail_report_for(subject)
activate R
R --> T : report { rewrite_justifications: [ { rule_label, <b>sigma</b>, <b>contractum</b> } ], is_complete }
deactivate R

note over T, R #FDE7D3
  STEP 1 — corrupt the report. Overwrite <b>sigma</b> (a redex LOCATOR) and, for binder-<latex>\beta</latex>,
  <b>contractum</b> (the retired host reduct) to NONSENSE. Leave ONLY the GATE fields
  valid: <b>rule_label</b> + <b>is_complete</b> (the two fields the MATCH path reads).
end note

T -[#C05621]> T : sigma := NONSENSE ;  contractum := NONSENSE\n(rule_label, is_complete kept valid)

T -> M : rho_net_match_invocation_from_dovetail_to(subject, corrupted_report, "OUT")
activate M
M -> M : gate reads ONLY rule_label + is_complete\nM-reflect the SUBJECT structurally\n(NOT the report sigma)
M --> T : invocation.call  =  network(automaton) || spread(subject)
deactivate M

T -> RHO : run(call), observe OUT
activate RHO
RHO -> RHO : spread subject on loc:/ac: ;\nautomaton LOCATES redex, CAPTURES <latex>\sigma'</latex> from the spread ;\nfire the sigma-receiver COMM
RHO -[#2F855A]-> OUT : OUT ! ( <b>Pair(B, A)</b> )
deactivate RHO

note over RHO, OUT #E6F4EA
  STEP 2 — observe. OUT = <b>Pair(B, A)</b>, re-sourced from the spread of the reflected
  subject. Had the path read the report <latex>\sigma</latex>, OUT would carry the NONSENSE
  (e.g. Pair(Pair(B,B), Pair(A,A))). It does not:  the reduct is the automaton's
  in-Rho capture + the reducer's firing, a genuine REPLACEMENT of the host matcher.
end note

T -[#2F855A]> OUT : assert OUT == Pair(B, A)
T -[#C05621]> OUT : assert OUT != NONSENSE  (report <latex>\sigma</latex> / contractum demonstrably unused)

legend right
|= Colour |= Meaning |
|<#C05621> orange | corruption / negative assertion (report input made unusable) |
|<#2F855A> green | correct reduct re-sourced from the spread + positive assertion |
endlegend
@enduml
